course: dictionary
lesson: 9634
title: Stuffy: stale air, a blocked nose, or a dull person
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one you need. «The Water Rat asks if it is very hot and stuffy, down in the hold.» The hold is inside a ship, a closed place with little fresh air, so stuffy means warm and stale.
explain: Stuffy can describe your body too. When you have a cold, your nose can feel blocked and hard to breathe through, so you have a stuffy nose. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the words around it?
explain: Stuffy can also describe a person. «Uncle Ben is a stuffy old man» means he is formal, old-fashioned and dull, and he does not like fun or change. The poem uses «frowst», which means to laze in a stuffy warm room, so context helps you understand a word you have never seen before.
fact: Stuffy means warm and stale, with not enough fresh air, when it describes a room.
fact: A stuffy nose is blocked, so it is hard to breathe through, often because of a cold.
fact: A stuffy person is old-fashioned, formal and boring, and does not like fun or change.
fact: Opening a window lets in fresh air and lets out stale air.
fact: «Frowst» means to laze in a stuffy warm room.
exercise: «The Water Rat asks if it is very hot and stuffy, down in the hold.» What does stuffy mean here? | *Warm air with not enough fresh air | A nose blocked by a cold | Full of soft cushions | Very cold and windy
exercise: Maya says, «I can't breathe through my nose, it's so stuffy with this cold.» What does stuffy mean? | *Blocked, so it is hard to breathe through the nose | Full of fresh sea air | Very wet and muddy | Old-fashioned and formal
exercise: «Uncle Ben is a stuffy old man who never likes games.» What does stuffy suggest about Uncle Ben? | Loud and funny | Blocked and hard to breathe | *Formal, old-fashioned and boring | Warm and sleepy
test: Why do scientists say opening a window helps a stuffy classroom? | It makes the room warmer and darker | *It lets in fresh air and lets out stale air | It makes the room smell of smoke
test: In the poem, «frowst» means what? | To read a large book by the fire | *To laze in a stuffy warm room | To dig a deep hole in the garden | To sweat a little after hard work
exam: Which sentence uses stuffy to mean old-fashioned and boring? | The air in the bus felt stuffy and hot. | My nose is stuffy, so I can't smell the soup. | *Grandma is so stuffy that she never lets us play loud music. | The hold of the ship was stuffy and dark.
